winemac: Park the last frame behind the metal layer during a hosted resize.

The client tears its swapchain down and rebuilds it on every size change, and
the metal layer has no contents until the first drawable at the new size is
presented.  Each resize step therefore flashed the layer's black background --
one full black frame per step, which an interactive drag turns into visible
strobing (measured: luma 0.0 frames in a 20-frame capture burst during a
stepped resize of steam's client, wine-debug-tools/flashmeter.sh).

Park the previous frame's contents in the container layer, stretched to the
new geometry, before moving the metal layer.  The metal layer covers it again
the moment it has a drawable, so the stale frame is only ever visible in the
gap the swapchain rebuild leaves.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
index 1de9f0a..8860465 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -4160,6 +4160,19 @@ - (void) setContainer:(CGRect)container frame:(CGRect)frame
     /* no implicit animation, a resize must land in one frame */
     [CATransaction begin];
     [CATransaction setDisableActions:YES];
+
+    /* the client tears its swapchain down and rebuilds it on resize, and the
+       metal layer has no contents until the first drawable at the new size is
+       presented; without a stale frame parked behind it, every resize step is
+       a black flash of the layer background.  the container shows the old
+       frame stretched into the gap and the metal layer covers it again as
+       soon as it has contents. */
+    if (o.contents)
+    {
+        c.contents = o.contents;
+        c.contentsGravity = kCAGravityResize;
+    }
+
     c.bounds = CGRectMake(0, 0, CGRectGetWidth(container), CGRectGetHeight(container));
     o.anchorPoint = CGPointMake(0, 0);
     o.bounds = CGRectMake(0, 0, CGRectGetWidth(frame), CGRectGetHeight(frame));
